+## Colours
+
+By default systemctl-tui picks sensible colours for light and dark terminals. To match your terminal theme, put a `config.toml` in the config directory (see `systemctl-tui --version`) or point at a file with `--config <path>`:
+
+```toml
+# All keys are optional; anything you leave out keeps the default.
+accent    = "#c5c0ff" # focused borders, active units, hints
+border    = "#4D415F" # unfocused panel borders
+selection = "#313245" # selected line background
+primary   = "#c5c0ff" # footer and help text
+```
+
+`SYSTEMCTL_TUI_CONFIG` overrides the config directory (or points straight at a config file).
+
 ## Remote hosts
 
 `systemctl-tui --host user@hostname` and `systemctl-tui --remote` manage a remote machine over SSH, no remote install needed.
